            <ArticleTitle>Catalytic Asymmetric 1,3-Dipolar Cycloaddition/Hydroamination Sequence: Expeditious Access to Enantioenriched Pyrroloisoquinoline Derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11238-11246</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b01927</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A three-step reaction sequence has been developed to prepare a variety of enantioenriched pyrroloisoquinoline derivatives. The process involves a catalytic asymmetric azomethine ylide 1,3-dipolar cycloaddition followed by an intramolecular AuI-catalyzed alkyne hydroamination and enamine reduction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
